   "text": "I read the structure region by region, then checked the three stereocentres against the wedges.\n\n**Macrocycle backbone** (going round the ring):\n- The left residue is an ornithine. Its \u03b1-carbon carries a wedged CH2CH2CH2NH-Boc chain and a ring NH. That NH is joined through a CH2 to C3 of a pyridine.\n- The pyridine C2 carries the ring sulfur. The sulfur is bonded to an aryl carbon that sits between a C\u2013F carbon and the carbon bearing the CH2.\n- The aryl ring has a CH2 (leading to the NH of the tryptophan amide), then C\u2013Br, two CH carbons, C\u2013F, and the C\u2013S carbon.\n- The left residue's C=O is bonded to the NH of the top residue.\n- The top residue is also an ornithine, with a wedged CH2CH2CH2NH-Boc chain. Its C=O is bonded to the N-methyl nitrogen of the tryptophan.\n- The tryptophan \u03b1-carbon carries a wedged CH2 to indole C3 and a C(=O)NH\u2013CH2-aryl amide. The indole nitrogen carries a Boc group.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned CIP priorities (N > C=O > CH2 > H) from the wedge geometry. All three stereocentres come out as S, consistent with L-amino acids. I then checked that the SMILES chirality tags (@@ for the left ornithine, @ for the other two) reproduce S at each centre.\n\nSMILES: CC(C)(C)OC(=O)NCCC[C@@H]1NCc2cccnc2Sc2c(F)ccc(Br)c2CNC(=O)[C@H](Cc2cn(C(=O)OC(C)(C)C)c3ccccc23)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(=O)OC(C)(C)C)NC1=O"
